(3177263, 442359, 656, '<td valign="top">Interesting that you used HDR, even though the clouds are still blown out, I like the orange and red palette of the grasses and rust, more than the sky or surrounding greenery.</td>', 'Interesting that you used HDR, even though the clouds are still blown out, I like the orange and red palette of the grasses and rust, more than the sky or surrounding greenery.', '2007-01-03 17:39:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3177266, 443277, 35804, '<td valign="top">Very interesting composition...the punches of oxide/pea soup green against the soft grays and whites works very nicely.</td>', 'Very interesting composition...the punches of oxide/pea soup green against the soft grays and whites works very nicely.', '2007-01-03 17:40:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(3177284, 443440, 656, '<td valign="top">Lovely location to shoot in.  My only issue is with the horizon distortion and the strong horizontal salt line so close to the edge of the frame in the bottom of the scene.  Moving that backwards or forwards would have made that bottom shape less static, perhaps.  Also the salt edge at the left is quite cramped into the edge of the frame - again more or less space would help with the balance of the shapes.  It can also be a really strong idea to find a rhythmic shape in the clouds or hills and try to find something to play off that in the foreground.  Works particularly well with such geometric and easily found shapes as presented here.  (e.g., the two hills coming down to the valley in the distance and something that reflected or played off that in the salt.</td>', 'Lovely location to shoot in.  My only issue is with the horizon distortion and the strong horizontal salt line so close to the edge of the frame in the bottom of the scene.  Moving that backwards or forwards would have made that bottom shape less static, perhaps.  Also the salt edge at the left is quite cramped into the edge of the frame - again more or less space would help with the balance of the shapes.  It can also be a really strong idea to find a rhythmic shape in the clouds or hills and try to find something to play off that in the foreground.  Works particularly well with such geometric and easily found shapes as presented here.  (e.g., the two hills coming down to the valley in the distance and something that reflected or played off that in the salt.', '2007-01-03 17:43:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3177289, 443643, 656, '<td valign="top">Seems like a lot of editing for the sake of editing, rather than in support of the idea of the shot.</td>', 'Seems like a lot of editing for the sake of editing, rather than in support of the idea of the shot.', '2007-01-03 17:44:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3177296, 441885, 35804, '<td valign="top">A refreshing piece of documentary work..."Lovers 4 Life"...a promising footnote and bit of hope...very nice.</td>', 'A refreshing piece of documentary work..."Lovers 4 Life"...a promising footnote and bit of hope...very nice.', '2007-01-03 17:45:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3177299, 442940, 656, '<td valign="top">at least the special effects are done for a purpose in this, which is in stark contrast to a lot of the entries</td>', 'at least the special effects are done for a purpose in this, which is in stark contrast to a lot of the entries', '2007-01-03 17:45:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3177308, 443545, 656, '<td valign="top">Could do with some cropping to better balance the ideas.  Currently very central subject and quite static, for something that is supposed to be awakening...</td>', 'Could do with some cropping to better balance the ideas.  Currently very central subject and quite static, for something that is supposed to be awakening...', '2007-01-03 17:46:44.000000', NULL, 1),
