(3184172, 442521, 53147, '<td valign="top">I think if you had put you in here somehow rather than the gull. But then I am a self portrait junkkie I guess. The gull just seems an odd fit. The colors and processing are pretty cool (the blur on the left seems a bit odd). Get on in there next time man - even if you were curled up into a ball lying on your side covered by a newspaper. Hey - maybe thats my next challenge entry right there. I will make sure to wear the derby. Good work Enzo.</td>', 'I think if you had put you in here somehow rather than the gull. But then I am a self portrait junkkie I guess. The gull just seems an odd fit. The colors and processing are pretty cool (the blur on the left seems a bit odd). Get on in there next time man - even if you were curled up into a ball lying on your side covered by a newspaper. Hey - maybe thats my next challenge entry right there. I will make sure to wear the derby. Good work Enzo.', '2007-01-05 07:11:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184176, 443555, 53147, '<td valign="top">Wow - way to go pulling out the detail fom your original image. I am still impressed when I see what people are able to do with a pic that I would have tossed in the recycle bin without a second thought. Well done!</td>', 'Wow - way to go pulling out the detail fom your original image. I am still impressed when I see what people are able to do with a pic that I would have tossed in the recycle bin without a second thought. Well done!', '2007-01-05 07:16:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184179, 443807, 53147, '<td valign="top">Hey Jimmy - at first glance this is a really nice picture (I dont have any issues with the frame). But as I look closer to the details I see littler circles all over the place. And not just a couple - full rows of circles layered on top of each other. At first I thought it might have been those solar glare circles that you may have added for effect but man there are alot - right through the bulk of your clouds. I wonder if my monitor is on some funky setting. A cool pic none the less but I thought you would be interested in what I am seeing.</td>', 'Hey Jimmy - at first glance this is a really nice picture (I dont have any issues with the frame). But as I look closer to the details I see littler circles all over the place. And not just a couple - full rows of circles layered on top of each other. At first I thought it might have been those solar glare circles that you may have added for effect but man there are alot - right through the bulk of your clouds. I wonder if my monitor is on some funky setting. A cool pic none the less but I thought you would be interested in what I am seeing.', '2007-01-05 07:20:47.000000', NULL, 0),
