(3184847, 443636, 47378, '<td valign="top">Wow, I guess this one really took a beating for the stretch to fit the challenge topic. I gave it a 7 because it''s a great shot, but apparently others didn''t think so.</td>', 'Wow, I guess this one really took a beating for the stretch to fit the challenge topic. I gave it a 7 because it''s a great shot, but apparently others didn''t think so.', '2007-01-05 12:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184855, 443663, 18367, '<td valign="top">I saw the image and thought I might know who took the photograph, and was absolutely certain once I read the caption.  I am convinced that I have read this somewhere, probably a poem.<br/> <br/>I do truly like this image although it does take time to gain a full appreciation for this type of artistry.  My only quibble is that I found the foreground a tad oversharpened, and wondered what those "Blotches" were at the top of the image.<br/> <br/>I do consider myself to be a rather harsh marker, but did give this image an 8.  Congraluations on pioneering this new Genre.<br/> <br/>Ray</td>', 'I saw the image and thought I might know who took the photograph, and was absolutely certain once I read the caption.  I am convinced that I have read this somewhere, probably a poem. I do truly like this image although it does take time to gain a full appreciation for this type of artistry.  My only quibble is that I found the foreground a tad oversharpened, and wondered what those "Blotches" were at the top of the image. I do consider myself to be a rather harsh marker, but did give this image an 8.  Congraluations on pioneering this new Genre. Ray', '2007-01-05 12:54:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184857, 443509, 30214, '<td valign="top">Marla,<br/>this is not a blend of three different photos (I rarely do such tricks they usually feel fake) - this is a single shot of a real scene, just three conversions from RAW at different exposure values to capture the huge dynamic range. But thanks for the comment!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 2mccs:</b></div><hr/><i> What a beautiful shot and a great blend of the 3 photos. I should have thought of that with the Badwater (salt formations) shot. I did do the HDR but I wish I had a better shot of the background mountains to blend with the foreground. Wonderful photo of an amazing part of the country </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Marla,this is not a blend of three different photos (I rarely do such tricks they usually feel fake) - this is a single shot of a real scene, just three conversions from RAW at different exposure values to capture the huge dynamic range. But thanks for the comment! Originally posted by 2mccs: What a beautiful shot and a great blend of the 3 photos. I should have thought of that with the Badwater (salt formations) shot. I did do the HDR but I wish I had a better shot of the background mountains to blend with the foreground. Wonderful photo of an amazing part of the country ', '2007-01-05 12:55:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184887, 441839, 44490, '<td valign="top">Timfy, great story in image and word, interesting texture to tie the images together.  Nicely done, and congratulations on another honorable mention.</td>', 'Timfy, great story in image and word, interesting texture to tie the images together.  Nicely done, and congratulations on another honorable mention.', '2007-01-05 13:08:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184928, 443625, 2158, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ursula:</b></div><hr/><i> What in the world are "koki pens"? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>They are felt tipped pens.</td>', 'Originally posted by ursula: What in the world are "koki pens"?   They are felt tipped pens.', '2007-01-05 13:23:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3184963, 442700, 29753, '<td valign="top">my favorite</td>', 'my favorite', '2007-01-05 13:33:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3185175, 443706, 66384, '<td valign="top">The thing that I find distracting in this image is the large negative space in the upper right quadrant of the picture caused by the straight line of the half moon leading directly down to the left bank of the fjord. And I am confused by the abstract black and white of the fjord vs the very realistic foreground with the boys/men.<br/> <br/>The odd thing is that those same things are what I like about the image. I just think I would like them in separate shots. The abstract of the fjord and moon would be good as one, and the boys/men would be good in another. Or the boys and moon without the fjord.<br/> <br/>I have no problem with the quality of the image on my monitor. Larus probably has a much finer setup than I do.</td>', 'The thing that I find distracting in this image is the large negative space in the upper right quadrant of the picture caused by the straight line of the half moon leading directly down to the left bank of the fjord. And I am confused by the abstract black and white of the fjord vs the very realistic foreground with the boys/men. The odd thing is that those same things are what I like about the image. I just think I would like them in separate shots. The abstract of the fjord and moon would be good as one, and the boys/men would be good in another. Or the boys and moon without the fjord. I have no problem with the quality of the image on my monitor. Larus probably has a much finer setup than I do.', '2007-01-05 14:39:42.000000', NULL, 0),
