(3185566, 443440, 656, '<td valign="top">One of my favourite shots in the challenge. <br/> <br/>The one thing I don''t quite see is the need for HDR because the light looks quite flat/ even in the scene already - would be interesting if you could post small versions of the 5 shots - it kinda looks like a single exposure would have done, something like the +1 exposure to keep the whites white but not blown out ?  I shot a lot of these myself and just adjusted the exposure until the highlights were well captured but not blown and it seems pretty similar, so I''d love to see the difference between the +1 and final shots if you don''t mind ?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-01-05 16:49:02.</i></td>', 'One of my favourite shots in the challenge.  The one thing I don''t quite see is the need for HDR because the light looks quite flat/ even in the scene already - would be interesting if you could post small versions of the 5 shots - it kinda looks like a single exposure would have done, something like the +1 exposure to keep the whites white but not blown out ?  I shot a lot of these myself and just adjusted the exposure until the highlights were well captured but not blown and it seems pretty similar, so I''d love to see the difference between the +1 and final shots if you don''t mind ?', '2007-01-05 16:47:27.000000', '2007-01-05 16:49:02.000000', 0),
